menu "PixelClip health (RTC watchdog, liveness)"

    config PIXELCLIP_RTC_WDT_TIMEOUT_S
        int "RTC watchdog timeout (s)"
        range 15 120
        default 40
        help
            The RTC watchdog keeps counting in light sleep (unlike the task watchdog) and is fed by the
            controller loop every 5 s while every required liveness source has checked in (health.h: player
            30 s, power task 15 s, and during a WiFi session the httpd task 30 s and the lwIP thread 15 s,
            the NimBLE host 30 s while BLE runs). If the chip sleeps without waking, or a source is silent,
            it resets the chip after this time (system reset; a full RTC reset 5 s later if that did not
            help). The boot log then says "reset reason RTCWDT_..." and names the silent source.

endmenu
